/-!
# Hereditary C⋆-subalgebras, generated hereditary subalgebras, and strictly positive elements

A nonunital `⋆`-subalgebra `B` of an ordered algebra `A` is *hereditary* if `0 ≤ a ≤ b` and
`b ∈ B` imply `a ∈ B`. In a C⋆-algebra, every closed two-sided ideal is hereditary (Blackadar
II.5.1.1(ii)), and a closed nonunital `⋆`-subalgebra `B` is hereditary if and only if
`b₁ * x * b₂ ∈ B` for all `b₁, b₂ ∈ B` and `x ∈ A`, or equivalently `b * x * b ∈ B` for all
nonnegative `b ∈ B` and `x ∈ A` (Blackadar II.5.3.1).

For any self-adjoint (in particular, nonnegative) element `a` of a C⋆-algebra `A`, the algebraic
corner `a * A * a` is a nonunital `⋆`-subalgebra whose topological closure `closure (a * A * a)`
is the smallest closed hereditary C⋆-subalgebra containing `a`. When `p` is a star projection,
`p * A * p` is already closed and equals `{x : A | p * x * p = x}`.

Finally, we distinguish *full* elements (those generating `A` as a closed two-sided ideal) from
*strictly positive* elements in the nonunital C⋆-algebra sense (nonnegative elements `a` with
`closure (a * A * a) = A`, Blackadar II.4.2.1). Every strictly positive element is full,
`closure (a * A * a) = A` is equivalent to `closure (a * A) = A`, and in a unital C⋆-algebra
this notion coincides with Mathlib's `IsStrictlyPositive` (`0 ≤ a ∧ IsUnit a`).

## Main declarations

* `NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.IsHereditary`: the heredity predicate `0 ≤ a ≤ b ∈ B → a ∈ B`, together
  with lattice and `comap` stability.
* `TwoSidedIdeal.mem_of_nonneg_of_le` and `TwoSidedIdeal.isHereditary_toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra`
  (plus `Ideal` counterparts): every closed two-sided ideal of a C⋆-algebra is hereditary.
* `NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.isHereditary_tfae`,
  `NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.isHereditary_iff_mul_mul_mem`, and
  `NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.isHereditary_iff_nonneg_mul_mul_mem`: the Blackadar II.5.3.1
  characterizations of closed hereditary C⋆-subalgebras.
* `TauCeti.cornerSubalgebra` and `TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.hereditarySubalgebra`: the algebraic corner
  `a * A * a` and closed hereditary C⋆-subalgebra `closure (a * A * a)` generated by a self-adjoint
  element `a`, with its universal property `hereditarySubalgebra_le_iff`.
* `TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.IsFull` and `TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.IsStrictlyPositive`: full elements and
  strictly positive elements of a possibly nonunital C⋆-algebra, with
  `IsStrictlyPositive.isFull`, `isStrictlyPositive_iff_dense_range_mul`, and the unital
  identification `isStrictlyPositive_iff_unital`.

## References

* Bruce Blackadar, *Operator Algebras: Theory of C*-Algebras and von Neumann Algebras*,
  II.4.2.1, II.5.1.1(ii), II.5.3.1.
* Gerard J. Murphy, *C*-Algebras and Operator Theory*, Section 3.2.
-/

public section

open Filter Topology
